The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. The reports say otherwise. They
were merged on one symptom, a wrong date, and they hold three different problems. Fixing the
parser will not close the ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. A parser fix leaves the form-hint reports and the one-day reports open.
</Callout>

## What the reports hold

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is computed from the export, one row per cause. Each cause now has its own ticket:

1. **Parser reads month first** ([issue 1](https://github.com/Mw-megadev/kb-4471/issues/1)).
   The shared parser reads every date month first; day-first tenants write the day first.
   This is the `parser` row; it includes the one-day reports below, which the desk counts where they are filed.
2. **Form hint says MM/DD/YYYY** ([issue 2](https://github.com/Mw-megadev/kb-4471/issues/2)).
   Day-first tenants on `booking-v3` type what the hint tells them. This is the `hint` row.
3. **Off by one day** ([issue 3](https://github.com/Mw-megadev/kb-4471/issues/3)).
   Not a month flip. These are the reports in the note under the table. They are also counted in the `parser` row, because they are filed there by tenant. Likely a timezone or day-boundary bug.

## Why one ticket looked right

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject. Intake also tags each
report from the reporter's browser. Both are guesses about the symptom. The cause depends on
the tenant: its locale and its booking form (`causes.ts`). The "tagged as" column shows intake
disagreeing with the cause in both rows.

## Since April

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## What to do

- Work the three tickets separately.
- Triage by cause, not by subject line. [The explorer](/kb/triage/dedupe) shows pairs with the
  same subject and different causes.
- Do not read "merged" as "one bug". Count by cause.

